brief: GGUF.MiRust.com now contains TinyRustLM, a zero-dependency Rust/WASM browser-local SLM runtime and UI with ADP1/ASP1/ALR1 runtime adapter apply, browser-routed ADP1/ASP1/ALR1 adapter-family stacks, browser-verified module-plan receipts, assembly traces, eval-case evidence checksum display, assembly eval-digest proof, fetched evidence-file integrity proof, and generated q4/q8/f32 selector roots. Model Breeding routes through durable research, report synthesis, short-term routes, checksum pointers, and concept lanes for heritable artifacts, mate selection, phenotype evidence, and local fit until source and tests prove concrete runtime support.
